        "comments": "The assembly fTriLus1.hap1.1 is based on 38x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Chromosomes 1 and 16 share a low level of homology and appear to be the sex chromosome pair. However, in the absence of concrete evidence, they have not been labelled as such. There is a large heterozygous inversion on Chromosome 24 from\n2.4 -6.5 Mbp.",
